v data-rid="2571a14a-0831-4f2f-a65c-35fafe666e6e" class="vy-r-170e8pl"><div data-rid="ff922019-b76c-4229-973e-effcb3c42d6f" class="vy-r-14fylu9"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="presentation" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:auto;max-height:100%" class="vy-r-3qq3yd" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 7.293l2.646-2.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708L8.707 8l2.647 2.646a.5.5 0 0 1-.708.708L8 8.707l-2.646 2.647a.5.5 0 0 1-.708-.708L7.293 8 4.646 5.354a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div><div data-rid="45cc9dbc-9428-45a3-bd00-dbb77066a3d9" class="vy-r-w8nula vy-alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><strong>Three Review Counts</strong>: 2,381, then 4,000+, then 15,340+, and no widget to check</p></span></div></div><div data-rid="4a6063a7-5fad-4d53-9d73-592d8a81b412" class="vy-r-lwogqz"><div data-rid="00eceaae-4e68-4e5f-b1c5-b8cf258f7ab8" class="vy-r-5jai1s"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="presentation" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:auto;max-height:100%" class="vy-r-1i894qj" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 7.293l2.646-2.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708L8.707 8l2.647 2.646a.5.5 0 0 1-.708.708L8 8.707l-2.646 2.647a.5.5 0 0 1-.708-.708L7.293 8 4.646 5.354a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div><div data-rid="1ddcecc0-4173-43c5-8506-9ffd70319b78" class="vy-r-fz3lpy vy-alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><strong>Sugar Based</strong>: 2 g of added sugar a serving, unlike the tinctures</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="ea78ce7c-8091-4a9e-9a41-b2a3d1481e16" class="vy-r-35iay9"><div data-rid="01d5e0e8-7f6e-48e9-93f8-1b6ba32361a8" class="vy-r-16upimq"><div data-rid="9289680c-1660-45c2-9435-828c480634a3" class="vy-r-v0566o vy-alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h3>The Verdict:</h3></span></div><div data-rid="c8c68193-71c4-4449-92c1-4386fb3e1a82" class="vy-r-1hdktjn vy-alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>I wanted this one to work out. Its panel prints 2,000 mg of a 50:1 mullein extract with nothing buried in a blend, and a pear gummy is a much easier daily habit than a dropper. Then I read the rest of the page. It advertises five compounds, names cordyceps, ginger, bromelain and lemon peel, and not one of those four shows up on the label I had just read.<br><br></p></span></div></div><div data-rid="1b36095e-1942-42d2-9045-434ddf14ebaf" class="vy-r-xt6i5p"><div data-rid="a2d323d3-c0da-4222-93e9-7b0e133d44f3" class="vy-r-1lkz5j4 vy-alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h3>The Bottom Line:</h3></span></div><div data-rid="8c2063cf-6747-435a-b239-9496dd89a9bb" class="vy-r-v9vsjc vy-alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>The gummy itself might be perfectly decent. What I could not get past is a page that contradicts its own ingredient list and its own star rating, then promises 60 days when the refund policy says 30. At $39, with an autoship ticked by default, I want the numbers to hold still first.<br></p></span></div></div><div data-rid="12b48caa-6695-460a-a9ac-a9889ccfaa00" class="vy-r-kk3tu0 vy-alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><em>Results are based on the product's published label and marketing and do not necessarily reflect typical results from use.</em></p></span></div></div></div><button data-rid="45fe0afa-9dfb-4b20-b17e-c0705e02ea83" class="vy-text vy-r-7w4otb vy-alchemy-rte"><div data-rid="46cfc081-7140-4fe7-9ad5-fb6c65e52805" class="vy-r-1misc29 vy-alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Learn More &#8594;</p></span></div></button></div></div><div data-rid="03eb96fe-5908-447d-be13-c1ef93bd266f" class="vy-r-nx7mex"><div data-rid="06286827-875b-41e3-9ce1-7efd33ecfa22" class="vy-r-1mdbgj2"><div data-rid="7c1d84ad-a3c2-4832-b78c-bd23ffd6e887" class="vy-r-1cvgyvq vy-alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h2>The Clear Winner: BetterLungs Mullein + Chlor